{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-MRSA, Antibiofilm, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (84.6%) to Dermaseptin-B5. A 20%, K 16%, GRAVY 0.18; Mol Wt 2606.073; Mol form: C118H195N30O33S1, Mol Ex. Coeff 5550. Structure: helical in TFE (50%)(CD). Activity: Broad spectrum, active against S. aureus NCTC 10788 (MIC 16 uM), MRSA NCTC 12493 (MIC 32 uM), E. faecalis NCTC 12697 (MIC 16 uM), Gram- E. coli NCTC 10418 (MIC 8 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC 16 uM), K. pneumoniae ATCC 43816 (MIC 8 uM), and C. albicans NCYC 1467 (MIC 64 uM). MBC is usually 2 fold higher than MIC. SAR: After changing residues 8 and 23 to K, the peptide became more helical, and more active (MIC 2-4) against the above microorganisms. MBIC (minimal biofilm inhibitory concentration) 8-32 against E. coli and MRSA. In vitro Toxicity: Low hemo.lytic activity (HC50) 128-256 uM. Edited 7/2021; 12/2024", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31635388", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Biomolecules. 2019 Oct 18;9(10). pii: E628. doi: 10.3390/biom9100628. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03133", "source_id": "AP03133", "source_numeric_id": "03133", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03133", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "A Novel Dermaseptin Isolated from the Skin Secretion of Phyllomedusa tarsius and Its Cationicity-Enhanced Analogue Exhibiting Effective Antimicrobial and Anti-Proliferative Activities", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
